            <ArticleTitle>The Self Care Assessment Schedule (SCAS)--II. Reliability and validity.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>203-14</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Evaluation of the SCAS in three groups of patients demonstrates high levels of test-retest reliability and satisfactory internal consistency. Multiple investigations of validity support the use of the SCAS as a measure of self care deficit which is related to social disability. The potential uses of the SCAS in clinical work and research are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
